    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0261" n="241" xml:id="pg241"/>

                <head>Mr. F. W. Seward. to Mr.
                        Geofroy</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 6, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communication of the 28th ultimo relative to certain duties exacted of
                    Messrs. Brulaton &amp; Co., of New Orleans, and, in reply, to inform you that I
                    have transmitted a translation thereof to the Secretary of the Treasury, who has
                    been requested to investigate the matter, with a view to the adoption of such
                    proceedings as the result may call for.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, a renewed assurance of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">L. de Geofroy,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
